        <item>
            <title>1.0.37 (2607031223)</title>
            <pubDate>2026-07-03 10:25:40</pubDate>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.6</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:version>260703.1223</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.37</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>180db Changelog — July 3, 2026</h3>
<h3>Stability</h3>
<ul>
<li>Fixed several crashes: moving tracks with nothing selected, pressing play on a restored window whose playlist had shrunk, and loading playlists with stale database entries.</li>
<li>Closing the license window with the red button no longer leaves the app stuck with no windows.</li>
<li>Pressing Stop exactly as a track ends no longer jumps to the next track on its own.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Playlists</h3>
<ul>
<li>Skipped and cycling track markers now survive reordering, deleting tracks, and app restarts — previously any playlist change silently wiped them.</li>
<li>Moving a non-contiguous selection now keeps the right tracks highlighted.</li>
<li>Re-importing files you already have no longer erases their titles, artists, and metadata.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Startup & Windows</h3>
<ul>
<li>The app now launches instantly when offline or on a slow network — no more waiting on the license server.</li>
<li>Window positions are saved reliably, even when you move a window and quit immediately.</li>
<li>Opening windows is faster (fewer database reads per window).</li>
</ul>
<h3>System Integration</h3>
<ul>
<li>Control Center now shows a live progress scrubber and updates when an album advances between tracks.</li>
<li>Opening an audio file from Finder into an empty window now imports and starts playing reliably.</li>
<li>Captured audio (Cmd+B) pasted as a file no longer disappears after 60 seconds.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Multi-Window</h3>
<ul>
<li>Right-click menus on a background window now act on that window — previously Pause or Remove Track could hit the wrong player.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Keyboard</h3>
<ul>
<li>Shortcuts like C (cue), M (mute), and S (shuffle) now work on non-QWERTY keyboard layouts.</li>
<li>Setting a cue at the very start of a track (0:00) now works like any other cue.</li>
<li>Raising the volume slider while muted now unmutes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Safety</h3>
<ul>
<li>Wipe Database now asks for confirmation before deleting anything — Return and Escape both cancel; the wipe requires an explicit click.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Performance</h3>
<ul>
<li>Large album covers no longer re-upload to the GPU on every interaction (big win with the DJ shader active).</li>
<li>Playlists with tracks that have no artwork no longer hammer the disk while scrolling.</li>
<li>Reduced idle background work: cached text measurements, smarter prefetch polling, batched playlist refreshes.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Under the Hood</h3>
<ul>
<li>Removed over 4,000 lines of dead code across the audio engine and app.</li>
<li>Build pipeline hardened: a failed Rust build can no longer silently ship a stale audio engine, and release builds now hard-fail if the update signature is missing.</li>
<li>New engine safety guards around cue points, decode threads, and device changes.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
            
